  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 1.3.1, package-lock.json says 1.2.0, package-lock.json packages[\"\"] says 1.2.0.",
        "  make version of ncmake bumps info.xml, composer.json and package.json and re-syncs package-lock.json in one step, so they cannot drift apart. ncmake's lint-version workflow fails a push or a pull request on exactly this drift. The App Store and the server read info.xml, npm and composer read their own manifest. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying more than one version number, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ],
      "covers": [
        "lint-version/version-drift"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "link-dead",
      "lines": [
        "5 links of appinfo/info.xml lead nowhere:",
        "  <screenshot> https://codeberg.org/fds2610/NC-Gantt/raw/branch/main/screenshots/gantt-evm-overview.png: HTTP 404",
        "  <screenshot> https://codeberg.org/fds2610/NC-Gantt/raw/branch/main/screenshots/gantt-resources-view.png: HTTP 404",
        "  <screenshot> https://codeberg.org/fds2610/NC-Gantt/raw/branch/main/screenshots/gantt-report-evm.png: HTTP 404",
        "  <screenshot> https://codeberg.org/fds2610/NC-Gantt/raw/branch/main/screenshots/gantt-deck-integration.png: HTTP 404",
        "  <screenshot> https://codeberg.org/fds2610/NC-Gantt/raw/branch/main/screenshots/gantt-deck-board-linked.png: HTTP 404",
        "  The App Store page shows these links as they are; a reader who follows one ends on an error page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 28 to 33; the oldest maintained major is 33 (the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 28 reaches below the oldest maintained major (33), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP floor stated once: composer.json requires php >=8.1; appinfo/info.xml declares no php dependency.",
        "  Nothing contradicts anything here. Stating it in both places is what keeps a composer install from resolving packages for a PHP the server will not run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "No Node version is stated: no engines.node, no .nvmrc, and no node-version in the installed workflows.",
        "  Whoever builds the app uses whatever Node they have, and a build that works on one machine is then not evidence for the next."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.js, superseded form), Stylelint (.stylelintrc.js), PHPUnit (phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.php).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.js: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "script-without-workflow",
      "lines": [
        "package.json declares the script lint, which no installed workflow runs.",
        "  The template lint-eslint of nextcloud/.github runs lint: make workflows-install W=lint-eslint",
        "  A check that no workflow runs on a pull request catches only what the contributor who remembers to run it catches."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "1 declared package is named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/initial-state.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 218 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (composer.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. An SPDX id there needs a <nextcloud> min-version of 31 or higher.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 3) and composer.lock in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines).",
        "  make reads GNUmakefile and never Makefile; it runs only with make -f <name>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "Every directory the shipped PHP reaches through __DIR__ and the frontend through linkTo is in the shipped file set."
      ]
    }
  ],
